Article 2 (Documents to Be Received upon Request for Assistance)
(1) Where the Minister of Foreign Affairs or another government representative under the Act on the Appointment and Powers of Government Representatives and Special Envoys (hereinafter referred to as a "government representative") or the minister in charge of a project receives a request for assistance from the government of a developing country, that government shall be required to submit the following documents: <Amended on March 23, 2013>
1. An application for assistance;
2. A statement detailing the request for assistance;
3. A project feasibility study report;
4. A project implementation plan;
5. Other documents necessary for review of the project.
(2) The government of a developing country shall submit the project feasibility study report under paragraph (1) 3 and the project implementation plan under paragraph (1) 4 before review of the project under Article 11 (1) 4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Economic Development Cooperation Fund Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Decree") commences.
